\**{c=red:NOTE:}** If you are having difficulties flagging this quest, it might just not appear as flagged in your quest log.{br}Carry on by skipping the {p:Walahra Temple} cutscene as well as the first cutscene with {n:Totoroon} and see if you can progress when trading a {i:Timeworn Talisman|Timeworn Talisman|2861} and food item.
=2 Walkthrough
* Enter the {p:Walahra Temple} in {p:Aht Urhgan Whitegate} at (J/K-8) for a cutscene.
* Speak to {n:Yoyoroon} in {z:Nashmau} in (G-6), upper level stalls. If you speak to Yoyoroon as a {p:Blue Mage}, you will have to change jobs and speak to him again. After the cutscene, you will receive a {@k}{k:Message from Yoyoroon}.

:* Not {n:Yuyuroon}, who is located almost directly in front of Yoyoroon but on the lower level.

* Obtain a {i:Timeworn Talisman|Timeworn Talisman|2861} from {m:Ephramadian Shades|Ephramadian Shade} in {z:Arrapago Reef} or {z:Caedarva Mire}.
** Recommend using Survival Guide to {z:Caedarva Mire} and riding west then south to find Shades there or even further into {z:Arrapago Reef} (where you did the Cutter Mission CS's)
** Alternatively, purchase and use an {i:Arrapago Ring|Arrapago Ring|26235} with 100 {p:Imperial standing accolades} from {n:Asrahd} at {p:Aht Urhgan Whitegate} (I-8). It will put you right next to some {m:Ephramadian Shades|Ephramadian Shade} near the Cutter.

:* Talismans obtained prior to starting this quest can be used.
:* Shades may be found west of the {z:Dvucca Isle Staging Point}, around (G-10).
:* Shades may also be found near the {p:Survival Guide} for Caedarva Mire.

* Trade the Timeworn Talisman and a {@i:Sutlac|5577} {i:Sutlac|Sutlac|5577}, {@i:Irmik Helvasi|5572} {i:Irmik Helvasi|Irmik Helvasi|5572}, **or even both** to Yoyoroon in Nashmau. There is a chance that his appraisal of the item will fail. Trading both at once along with the talisman gives the highest chance for success.

:* The food can be purchased from {n:Fayeewah} and {n:Yafaaf} at the Shararat Teahouse in Whitegate.
:* Yoyoroon will not accept {i:Sutlac +1|Sutlac +1|5578} or {i:Irmik Helvasi +1|Irmik Helvasi +1|5573}.
:* Should the appraisal fail, you will have to obtain another Timeworn Talisman as well as any food items that you traded him.

* Should your appraisal succeed, you will have to zone and talk to Yoyoroon again to receive the {@k}{k:Talisman of the rebel gods}.
* Enter the Walahra Temple in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at (J/K-8) for a cutscene to receive the {@k}{k:Talisman key}.
** If you do not get a cutscene, inspect the {p:Imperial Whitegate} instead.
** **{c=red:NOTE:}** For any subsequent attempts, you will need to bring a new Talisman of the rebel gods directly to the Imperial Whitegate door (L-8/9).
* Enter {z:Hazhalm Testing Grounds} and examine the **Entry Gate** to view a cutscene.
** This is the same area as {p:Einherjar}. The quickest way is to use the {z:Caedarva Mire} {p:Home Point}.
* Examine the Entry Gate again to enter a BCNM.

:* **{c=red:Warning:}** **{p:Trust Magic} CANNOT be used in this BCNM.**
:* Your opponent will be {p:Odin Prime}, he can cast spells like Paralyze, Dispelga, and elemental magic.
:* Odin Prime can also spawn up to 3 Odin Images.
:* At a low percentage, Odin can use Zantetsuken if he stays alive for an extended period of time.

* After winning the battle, you will enter a cutscene where you will choose your reward.
* Examine {p:Imperial Whitegate} at {p:Aht Urhgan Whitegate} (L-8/9) for a cutscene to complete the quest.

:* If you receive the Trust quest cutscene for Trust: Nashmeira, finish the cutscene, then re-examine the gate to complete THIS quest.

